    "body": "Data for the fix (read from the run's gate-logs artifact, `750-app_suites_mcp_setup_moves.log`), nothing changed by me:\n\n```\npanicked at crates/app/tests/mcp_setup_moves.rs:98:5:\nassertion `left == right` failed: undo restores the setup in place\n  left: [\"Front\", \"Back\"]\n right: [\"Back\", \"Front\"]\n```\n\n#3485 (merged as `edcbfe4dd`) lists setups in creation order instead of name order, by design. After `delete_setup` of Front and an undo, Front is restored at its original (first) place, which is \"in place\" under the new order. The assert at line 97-98 still expects name order, and its comment says \"Setups list in name order ... (#1362)\". So this looks like a stale test expectation, not a product regression: the expected value becomes `[\"Front\", \"Back\"]` and the comment should cite #3485's creation order. The run of `81861c994` just before it was green.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
